<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nebuchadnezzar II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 562 BCE</span> · Also known as Nebuchadnezzar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nebuchadnezzar II was the most famous king of the Chaldean or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaldean-empire">Neo-Babylonian Empire</a>, who died in 562 BCE. As crown prince he defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> at Carchemish in 605 BCE, securing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a>. As king he captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>, rebuilt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> on a grand scale and invested in canals, making his reign the defining era of the empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nebuchadnezzar-ii.jpg" alt="Nebuchadnezzar II" width="320" height="297" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nebuchadnezzar_II_crop.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
